                    <p class=" coming-soon-regular" style="background-color: rgba(151, 240, 42, 0.13);">
                        <strong>Algorithm for the addition of two points: P + Q<br><br></strong>
(a) If P = O, then P + Q = Q.<br>
(b) Otherwise, if Q = O, then P + Q = P.<br>
(c) Otherwise, write P = (x&#8321;, y&#8321;) and Q = (x&#8322;, y&#8322;).<br>
(d) If x&#8321; = x&#8322; and y&#8321; = &minus;y&#8322;, then P + Q = O.<br>
(e) Otherwise:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(e1) If P &ne; Q: &lambda; = (y&#8322; &minus; y&#8321;) / (x&#8322; &minus; x&#8321;)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(e2) If P = Q: &lambda; = (3x&#8321;&sup2; + a) / (2y&#8321;)<br>
(f) x&#8323; = &lambda;&sup2; &minus; x&#8321; &minus; x&#8322;<br>
(h) y&#8323; = &lambda;(x&#8321; &minus; x&#8323;) &minus; y&#8321;<br>
(i) P + Q = (x&#8323;, y&#8323;)<br>
                    </p>


