                    <p class=" coming-soon-regular" style="background-color: rgba(151, 240, 42, 0.13);">
                        <strong>Double and Add algorithm for the scalar multiplication<<br><br></strong>

Input: P &isin; E(F<sub>p</sub>) and an integer n &gt; 0<br>
Output: Q = [n]P &isin; E(F<sub>p</sub>)<br><br>

1. Set Q = P and R = O.<br>
2. Loop while n &gt; 0.<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;3. If n &equiv; 1 mod 2, set R = R + Q.<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;4. Set Q = [2]Q and n = &lfloor;n / 2&rfloor;.<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;5. If n &gt; 0, continue with loop at Step 2.<br>
6. Return the point R, which equals [n]P.<br>
                    </p>


                    <p class=" coming-soon-regular">
