                <p class=" coming-soon-regular fw-bold underline"><br>10. ProSign3</p>
                <p class=" coming-soon-regular">
                    This is my secure timestamp signing server. Only if you can produce a signature for "unlock" can you learn more.<br>

                    <a href="https://cryptohack.org/static/challenges/13381_7fd5a5da326879dc4a3995cad969a165.py">13381.py</a>
                </p>
                <p class=" coming-soon-regular" style="background-color: rgba(151, 240, 42, 0.13);">
                    <strong>Signing</strong><br>
EC equation, <span style="color:blue;">G</span> fixed<br>
<span style="color:darkgreen;">d<sub>B</sub></span><span style="color:blue;">G</span> -> Bob's private key <br>
P<sub style="color:darkgreen;">B</sub> = <span style="color:darkgreen;">d<sub>B</sub></span> -> Bob's public key<br><br>
<span style="color:purple;">m</span> -> message<br>
<span style="color:orange;">z</span> -> hash(message)<br>
<br>
<span style="color:brown;">n</span> -> order of generator <span style="color:blue;">G</span><br>
<br>
<span style="color:red;">k</span> ∈ [1, n - 1] chosen randomly by Bob<br>
<span style="color:red;">k</span><span style="color:blue;">G</span> is computed, kg = (x1,y1)<br>
<span style="color:teal;">r</span> = x1 (mod n)<br>
<span style="color:maroon;">s</span> = <span style="color:red;">k</span><sup>-1</sup>(<span style="color:orange;">z</span> + <span style="color:teal;">r</span><span style="color:darkgreen;">d<sub>B</sub></span>)<br>
<br>
signature = (<span style="color:teal;">r</span>, <span style="color:maroon;">s</span>)<br>
<br>

<strong>Verification</strong><br>
u<sub>1</sub> = <span style="color:orange;">z</span><span style="color:maroon;">s</span><sup>-1</sup> mod n<br>
u<sub>2</sub> = <span style="color:teal;">r</span><span style="color:maroon;">s</span><sup>-1</sup> mod n<br>
<br>
u<sub>1</sub><span style="color:blue;">G</span> + u<sub>2</sub>P<sub style="color:darkgreen;">B</sub> = (x1, y1)<br>
valid signature: <span style="color:teal;">r</span> ≡ x1<br>
<br>

